1
00:00:05,956 --> 00:00:06,956
Hi, Grandpa.

2
00:00:06,956 --> 00:00:08,934
Hi, Robbie.

3
00:00:08,934 --> 00:00:10,294
Can I help?

4
00:00:10,294 --> 00:00:11,912
Yes, indeed.

5
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:14,890
Hand me two eggs from the refrigerator,

6
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:17,868
and I'll make you two fried eggs.

7
00:00:17,868 --> 00:00:20,846
How about some bacon?

8
00:00:20,846 --> 00:00:23,824
I made enough for an army.

9
00:00:23,824 --> 00:00:26,802
You going to the baseball game today?

10
00:00:26,802 --> 00:00:32,080
It's a perfect day for it--a little cloudy but nice and warm.

11
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:34,058
Dad and I were planning to go to the game,

12
00:00:34,058 --> 00:00:35,736
but he has to work today,

13
00:00:35,736 --> 00:00:37,736
and my friends don't want to go.

14
00:00:37,736 --> 00:00:39,202
It's not an important game, anyway.

15
00:00:39,202 --> 00:00:42,165
Do you have any other plans for the day?

16
00:00:42,165 --> 00:00:44,669
I'll work on my computer.

17
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:47,647
I have a new math program, and I want to learn how to use it.

18
00:00:47,647 --> 00:00:49,011
Maybe you can teach me

19
00:00:49,011 --> 00:00:51,425
how to work on a computer someday.

20
00:00:51,425 --> 00:00:55,392
Anytime. It's really easy, but, like anything,

21
00:00:55,392 --> 00:00:59,559
you need to work at it, Grandpa.

22
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:01,159
This bacon is great.

23
00:01:01,159 --> 00:01:02,537
I love crispy bacon.

24
00:01:02,537 --> 00:01:05,515
Oh, what are you doing tomorrow?

25
00:01:05,515 --> 00:01:08,493
Nothing much.

26
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:14,231
Well, maybe your dad and I could take you fishing with us.

27
00:01:14,231 --> 00:01:15,521
I'd like that, but ...

28
00:01:15,521 --> 00:01:16,593
But what?

29
00:01:16,593 --> 00:01:19,094
But Dad is always so busy.

30
00:01:19,094 --> 00:01:25,223
Well, can you come fishing with me tomorrow?

31
00:01:25,223 --> 00:01:27,028
Sure, I can.

32
00:01:27,028 --> 00:01:32,317
Robbie says you can't take him to the game today.

33
00:01:32,317 --> 00:01:34,317
I really feel bad about it,

34
00:01:34,317 --> 00:01:36,406
but they need me at the hospital today,

35
00:01:36,406 --> 00:01:37,295
in the children's ward.

36
00:01:37,295 --> 00:01:38,273
I understand.

37
00:01:38,273 --> 00:01:42,108
Maybe we can spend some time together next weekend.

38
00:01:42,108 --> 00:01:42,537
Definitely.

39
00:01:42,537 --> 00:01:43,394
We should.

40
00:01:43,394 --> 00:01:46,029
You and Robbie and me.

41
00:01:46,029 --> 00:01:48,839
Remember our first fishing trip?

42
00:01:48,839 --> 00:01:50,852
I sure do....

43
00:01:50,852 --> 00:01:54,555
Well, I've got to run, Dad.

44
00:01:54,555 --> 00:01:56,807
See you later.

45
00:01:56,807 --> 00:01:59,118
Going fishing?

46
00:01:59,118 --> 00:02:03,086
I'm thinking about it....

47
00:02:03,086 --> 00:02:03,286
So, how's work?

48
00:02:03,086 --> 00:02:03,810
Oh, the usual problems.

49
00:02:03,810 --> 00:02:08,512
You're working pretty hard these days.

50
00:02:08,512 --> 00:02:10,352
I guess I am.

51
00:02:10,352 --> 00:02:15,508
When did you last go fishing with Robbie?

52
00:02:15,508 --> 00:02:16,986
I remember exactly.

53
00:02:16,986 --> 00:02:23,232
It was on his birthday, June second, two years ago.

54
00:02:23,232 --> 00:02:24,392
We didn't catch anything.

55
00:02:24,392 --> 00:02:26,585
Remember our fishing trips?

56
00:02:26,585 --> 00:02:29,648
Yes. I loved them.

57
00:02:29,648 --> 00:02:33,396
Remember catching your first fish?

58
00:02:33,396 --> 00:02:38,856
How can I forget?

59
00:02:38,856 --> 00:02:42,310
I fell out of the boat!

60
00:02:42,310 --> 00:02:47,766
We had some good times together.

61
00:02:47,766 --> 00:02:49,266
Yes, we did.

62
00:02:49,266 --> 00:02:53,389
Maybe we should do it again.

63
00:02:53,389 --> 00:02:54,389
How about tomorrow?

64
00:02:54,389 --> 00:02:59,378
Don't you have to work?

65
00:02:59,378 --> 00:03:01,128
My paper work will wait.

66
00:03:01,128 --> 00:03:03,344
Oh, Robbie will be thrilled.

67
00:03:03,344 --> 00:03:05,134
I am, too, Son.

68
00:03:05,134 --> 00:03:09,345
I want to spend more time with Robbie.

69
00:03:09,345 --> 00:03:09,692
Tomorrow.

70
00:03:09,692 --> 00:03:12,865
It'll be like old times for you and me.

71
00:03:12,865 --> 00:03:15,167
And Robbie will love it.

72
00:03:15,167 --> 00:03:19,065
Well, what's the weather going to be like?

73
00:03:19,065 --> 00:03:25,479
Radio says sunny and mild.

74
00:03:25,479 --> 00:03:31,435
Well, I'll tell Robbie.

75
00:03:31,435 --> 00:03:35,693
And thanks, Dad.

76
00:03:35,693 --> 00:03:37,391
Don't thank me.

77
00:03:37,391 --> 00:03:40,391
I'm just being a grandfather.
